<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wir sind des Geyers schwarzer Haufen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">poem <a href="/years/1888">1888</a>; melody <a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Wir sind des Geyers schwarzer Haufen&quot; (&quot;We Are Geyer's Black Band&quot;) is a German marching song of the years between the world wars. Its words come from the poem &quot;Ich bin der arme Konrad&quot;, written in 1888 by the Bavarian poet and artillery officer Heinrich von Reder, and its melody was arranged by the songwriter Fritz Sotke in 1919. The song looks back to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-peasants-war">German Peasants' War</a> of 1525.</p></div>
